detail:
A soft lock is presence, never a log line.
```js
presence {client, state: {user: "mike", editing: "content.p9"}}
// Room.locks: path -> {client, user, at}
// It ends on blur, or 30 s after presence stops.
new List({…, lock: "warn" | "refuse"})
```
An op under a path someone else holds: **warn** (the default) writes it and tells the writer; **refuse** rejects it with `{why: "locked", by}`. The UI shows "Mike is editing". The item tool tells an agent who holds the path.

You asked for simple edit locks; CRDTs are priority 5 (Yjs for a rich-text field, in phase 5).

